# Force LF on checkout for every text file, on every platform.
#
# Without this, git on Windows checks out with CRLF (core.autocrlf=true by
# default). That changes the bytes on disk, so:
#   * MANIFEST.sha256 verification fails on a Windows clone;
#   * the "committed case tree matches the generator" test fails, because the
#     generators write LF explicitly (newline="\n") while the checkout has CRLF.
#
# It does NOT affect the determinism claim: the canonical payload hash is computed
# over parsed JSON re-serialized under RFC 8785, so line endings never reach it.
# That is why the cross-platform determinism workflow passed on Windows even while
# the byte-comparison test did not.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.json   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.sql    text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.csv    text eol=lf
*.cff    text eol=lf
*.lock   text eol=lf
*.sha256 text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

*.docx   binary
*.pdf    binary
